{
  "title": "[compile][cudagraphs] Fail or loud warning with excessive rerecording",
  "issue_id": "162299",
  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nIn some cases (like re-recording on symint), cudagraph can end up with excessive re-recording. For an end user, this is completely silent, and at the end they see very bad speedups. \n\nIt gives an impression that torch.compile as a whole was bad. But if they just disabled cudagraph, they would still be able to reap large benefits. \n\nI saw this in transfomers repo where they had reduce-overhead by default. More background is that  `transformers` users control compile by just using a flag, and they have no idea that cudagraphs is turned ON, the compile call is hidden from the user. This can be a common pattern in many other tools as well. More details at https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HzcKdxjuz4SniEq-5h56FyRAAKPlx_YXiZClE4US2q4/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.r48wy68nhevn\n\nTherefore, we must raise loud warning or consider even failing hard. \n\n\ncc @mcarilli @ezyang @eellison @penguinwu @BoyuanFeng @chauhang \n \n\n### Error logs\n\n_No response_\n\n### Versions\n\nNA",
